;;; A `:where` pair beside a `:match`'s conjuncts is dropped, so the rule
;;; fires without its guard — regression `where-in-and`
;;; (`corpus/regressions.toml`).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two `p` facts and a rule whose `:match` writes `:where (neq ?x a)` beside
;;; its premise `(p ?x)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Each form takes a closed list of keywords, and a term takes none
;;; (Q-M1e2.28), so `:where` is refused wherever it is written: the program
;;; is refused at the parse, at the keyword, and every command that reads it
;;; exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `ec004a48` (the engine `916d97ac`'s), release and debug alike: the
;;; pair was dropped, so `r` fired for every `p`: root derived `(q a)` and
;;; `(q b)`, with no line (`ein saturate FILE --dump`), and R was four states
;;; over the candidates `(hit a)` and `(hit b)`, exit 0 (`ein solve FILE`,
;;; `ein oracle FILE`).
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;

(relation p Node) (relation q Node) (relation hit Node)
(p a) (p b)
(rule r () :match (and (p ?x) :where (neq ?x a)) :assert (q ?x))
